{"id":"10205c9c4c85a35d","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md","title":"Symmetric Operator","display":"df-symmetric-operator — Symmetric Operator","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-symmetric-operator","aliases":["58-df-symmetric-operator","Symmetric Operator"],"display":"df-symmetric-operator — Symmetric Operator","depends_on":["[[58-df-hilbert-space]]","[[58-df-linear-map]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-symmetric-operator"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-symmetric-operator</span><span>Symmetric Operator</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-symmetric-operator — Symmetric Operator"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"58-df-hilbert-space\">58-df-hilbert-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f67456d74b418241\" href=\"?note=f67456d74b418241\" title=\"58-df-linear-map\">58-df-linear-map</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,D,H,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H\\in V\">\\(A,D,H,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H\\in V\\)</span> (operator, domain, and Hilbert/vector-space structures)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\)</span> (Hilbert-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"58-df-hilbert-space\">58-df-hilbert-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S\\)</span> (fully explicit linear-map predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"f67456d74b418241\" href=\"?note=f67456d74b418241\" title=\"58-df-linear-map\">58-df-linear-map</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SymmetricOperatorStructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SymmetricOperatorStructure}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SymmetricOperator}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SymmetricOperator}_S\\)</span> (explicit predicate and Hilbert-carrier projection)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}operator\\text{-}explicit} \\vdash \\mathrm{SymmetricOperatorStructure}_S(A,D,H,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H)\\leftrightarrow\\left[\\begin{aligned}&amp;k\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H)\\land D\\subseteq H\\land\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(A,D,H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H)\\\\&amp;\\land\\forall y\\in H\\;\\bigl((\\forall x\\in D\\;B_H(x,y)=0)\\to y=0_H\\bigr)\\land\\forall x,y\\in D\\;B_H(A(x),y)=B_H(x,A(y))\\end{aligned}\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}operator\\text{-}explicit} \\vdash \\mathrm{SymmetricOperatorStructure}_S(A,D,H,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H)\\leftrightarrow\\left[\\begin{aligned}&amp;k\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H)\\land D\\subseteq H\\land\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(A,D,H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H)\\\\&amp;\\land\\forall y\\in H\\;\\bigl((\\forall x\\in D\\;B_H(x,y)=0)\\to y=0_H\\bigr)\\land\\forall x,y\\in D\\;B_H(A(x),y)=B_H(x,A(y))\\end{aligned}\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}operator\\text{-}projection} \\vdash \\mathrm{SymmetricOperator}_S(A,H)\\leftrightarrow\\exists D,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H\\in V\\;\\mathrm{SymmetricOperatorStructure}_S(A,D,H,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}operator\\text{-}projection} \\vdash \\mathrm{SymmetricOperator}_S(A,H)\\leftrightarrow\\exists D,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H\\in V\\;\\mathrm{SymmetricOperatorStructure}_S(A,D,H,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A symmetric operator is a densely defined linear operator satisfying <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle Ax,y\\rangle=\\langle x,Ay\\rangle\">\\(\\langle Ax,y\\rangle=\\langle x,Ay\\rangle\\)</span> on its domain. Density is expressed by trivial orthogonal complement, avoiding the unrelated transitive-set closure operator.</li>\n<li>Self-adjoint: symmetric + domain equal to full domain of adjoint; crucial for spectral theorem</li>\n<li>Deficiency indices: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n_{\\pm} = \\dim \\ker(A^* \\mp iI)\">\\(n_{\\pm} = \\dim \\ker(A^* \\mp iI)\\)</span>; determine extension possibilities</li>\n<li>Stone's theorem: 1-parameter unitary groups <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leftrightarrow\">\\(\\leftrightarrow\\)</span> self-adjoint generators</li>\n<li>von Neumann: symmetric operator with equal deficiency indices has self-adjoint extensions</li>\n<li>Self-adjointness and essential self-adjointness are downstream predicates.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reed and Simon, Methods of Mathematical Physics Vol. 1</li>\n<li>Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics</li>\n<li>Kato, Perturbation Theory for Linear Operators</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-hilbert-space","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-hilbert-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-linear-map","status":"resolved","id":"f67456d74b418241","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-linear-map]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-hilbert-space","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S$ (Hilbert-space predicate, see [[58-df-hilbert-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-linear-map","status":"resolved","id":"f67456d74b418241","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S$ (fully explicit linear-map predicate, see [[58-df-linear-map]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A,D,H,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SymmetricOperatorStructure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SymmetricOperator}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}operator\\text{-}explicit} \\vdash \\mathrm{SymmetricOperatorStructure}_S(A,D,H,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H)\\leftrightarrow\\left[\\begin{aligned}&k\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H)\\land D\\subseteq H\\land\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(A,D,H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H)\\\\&\\land\\forall y\\in H\\;\\bigl((\\forall x\\in D\\;B_H(x,y)=0)\\to y=0_H\\bigr)\\land\\forall x,y\\in D\\;B_H(A(x),y)=B_H(x,A(y))\\end{aligned}\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}operator\\text{-}projection} \\vdash \\mathrm{SymmetricOperator}_S(A,H)\\leftrightarrow\\exists D,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H\\in V\\;\\mathrm{SymmetricOperatorStructure}_S(A,D,H,B_H,k,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H)","display":true},{"tex":"\\langle Ax,y\\rangle=\\langle x,Ay\\rangle","display":false},{"tex":"n_{\\pm} = \\dim \\ker(A^* \\mp iI)","display":false},{"tex":"\\leftrightarrow","display":false}],"bytes":2373,"backlinks":[{"id":"93a99642b1c854e4","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Symmetric}_H$ (symmetric-operator predicate, see [[../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md]])"},{"id":"056f7b0dff6c7aee","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{SymmetricOperatorStructure}_S(T,D,H,B,\\mathbb C,+_D,\\odot_D,+_H,\\odot_H)$ (see [[58-df-symmetric-operator]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1276","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md|58-df-symmetric-operator]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["b70ce791d5b1a19b","f67456d74b418241"]}